<title>
Audio / Navigation Unit Removal and Installation
</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLBA0C9F06001003">
<title>
Removal
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Do not pull out the navigation unit (2) by holding on to the screen of the navigation unit as it may damage the navigation unit.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Disconnect negative (–) cable at battery.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove center ventilation louver. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLBA0C7226034"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove two mounting screws (1) from navigation unit bracket (3).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFBA0A9F0031.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "58.472mm" ver = "01" gw = "156" gh = "149"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
While removing navigation unit (1), pull out the unit by holding on to the bracket (2) as shown in the figure.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILBA0A9F0003.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "63.431mm" ver = "01" gw = "233" gh = "163"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Disconnect connectors (3) to remove the navigation unit.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILBA0A9F0004.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "70.992mm" ver = "01" gw = "234" gh = "185"/>
